== result (done, 129.1s)

## Spring vs summer support review

Reader-b could not open the summer document, so reader-a read both. Spring figures come from spring-review.md and summer figures from summer-review.md. The shared-themes flowchart is stored as art:d3bfc3ad6226.

### What improved (changed)
| Theme | Spring (spring-review.md) | Summer (summer-review.md) |
|---|---|---|
| Requests answered | "4,120 requests" (March–May), "up from 3,380 in winter" | "4,610 requests" (June–August) |
| Median first reply time | "3 hours 10 minutes" against a goal of "2 hours" | "fell to 1 hour 55 minutes", inside the "2 hour goal" for the first time |
| Account access | Requests "doubled" after the 14 April login change. Plan was five articles. | "Five account access articles" shipped in June. Requests "fell from 610 to 240 a month". |
| Weekend coverage | "two volunteers" kept Monday's backlog "under 90 requests". Plan was a shared on-call rotation. | The rotation replaced volunteers. Nobody worked more than "two weekends". |

### What did not improve (unchanged or new)
- **Hiring (unchanged):** Spring said replacements started only in late May and planned one more hire. Summer says the hiring plan slipped and the position is "still open".
- **Billing questions (new problem):** In spring, help articles cut repeat billing questions by "about a third". In summer, July's pricing change brought "380 billing questions in one week".
- **Customer satisfaction (new gap):** Summer says it is not tracked.
- Neither document explicitly lists anything as unchanged. The hiring item is my reading of the two documents.

### What the team should do next
Neither document names an owner for any of these actions, so the team needs to assign one for each.
1. **Fill the open position.** This is the carry-over from spring. Owner: to be assigned, for example the support lead.
2. **Prepare billing articles before any pricing change.** This is from summer-review.md. Owner: to be assigned.
3. **Start measuring customer satisfaction.** This is from summer-review.md. Owner: to be assigned.
4. **Hold the reply-time gain.** Reply time is only 5 minutes inside the goal. Neither document gives a step for this, so this one is my suggestion. Owner: to be assigned.

